ere were any reasons for this other than his predecessor\'s wish that it should be done, and it is paradoxical that al-Mahdl Ahmad, who was the strictest Hadawi of the early Qasimi imams, should have followed through with this order since it ran so counter to his school\'s teachings.” '}], {'usage.total_tokens': 912, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 855})
