ribal allies.”  “The Rasulids continued the Ayyubid policy of promoting the cause of Sunni Islam in the territories under their domination. As a result, the traditions of Sunni Islam became firmly established in their kingdom at a time when Shia Islam was being promoted in the mountainous interior of North Yemen by their rivals, the Zaydi Imams. Since the Rasulids were followers of Imam Shafi’i, the Shafi’ite brand of Sunni Islam became state religion.” '}], {'usage.total_tokens': 933, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 858})
