nism [a sect of Zoroastrianism/Mazdeism], which included some Hellenistic and Indian Buddhist influences. There was also a religious tolerance towards other cults (such as Nestorianism and Manichaeism).” '}], {'usage.total_tokens': 880, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 808})
