ame Supreme God. they can hardly be described as forming different sects.” <br>"the popular Hinduism i. e. the religion of the masses of our period [the Rashtrakutas]. This religion, may be described as the Smarta Pauranic religion.”  The following suggests that about a third of the population were Jain: “[o]ur period produced a galaxy of Jain authors and preachers whose literary and missionary activities must have produced a considerable effect, helped as they were by royal patronage. It is very probable that at least one third of the total population of the Deccan of our period was following the gospel of Mahavira.” '}], {'usage.total_tokens': 948, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 892})
