e parts of Asia Minor that lasted straight into the tenth century. Any discussion of the complex pattern of cultural adaption must begin in the late fourth and fifth centuries, when it becomes possible to speak seriously of a rural Christian epigraphy, and when literary sources of monastic provenance begin to appear.” '}], {'usage.total_tokens': 864, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 760})
