t not incised, oracle bones, mostly the scapula from pig, ox, sheep, and deer, were recovered from two sites north of the Songshan mountains, the large site of Miaodian, and the smaller site of Xiaopangou. They also were found at two major sites in the south: the large site of Wadian and the walled site of Haojiatai. One ox scapula found at Xiaopangou had more than 30 heating marks, presumably made for divination. "Finally, earlier and simpler forms of rituals known in the later historical period seem to have begun during the Wangwan III period. A good example is the pottery lie gu 列觚, a ranked set of gu 觚 goblets excavated at the large site of Wadian. This was a set of goblets of decreasing sizes similar to the lie ding 列鼎 sets of tripods found in later Shang and Zhou dynasty contexts." '}], {'usage.total_tokens': 1011, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 928})
